collisions and that if you want you can go through the game without having to face all the enemies in the game and a certain level of interactions with the world to make it feel special and not like a game as linear as certain one-person-made published games on <strong>STEAM</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Flaws and limitations</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >*The melee gameplay is simple, but effective at breaking certain objects. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >*Movement not so natural with keyboard, with controller it looks more natural </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >*Minor bug in <strong>VALVE</strong> code,\u00a0The weapon is shown to be jumping in an area where it shouldn't be.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >*Scenes can only be skipped when starting a new chapter from scratch</p>",
